            <note corresp="#d174-f2" n="2" xml:id="d174-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 1, <ref target="#pg1776">p. 1776</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d174-f3" n="3" xml:id="d174-f3-content">
                <p>Despatch 8 from Calcutta, not printed, reported Shakabpa’s account of what he had
                    learned from the Tibetan Delegates about their experiences in Peking
                    (793B.00/7–951).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d174-f4" n="4" xml:id="d174-f4-content">
                <p>Telegram 117 from Calcutta, not printed, conveyed a report that the Tibetan
                    Government planned to negotiate in Lhasa with the Chinese Delegation, that the
                    Dalai Lama might leave, if the Chinese insisted on bringing more troops to
                    Tibet, and that no word had been received from the Indian Government concerning
                    asylum for the Dalai Lama (793B.00/8–1351).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
